; A cross-reference reached through a union, inside a container's child.
; The shape PNGine reported (docs/plans/asks/19-*.md): `(box …)` is a
; container whose positional children are the ordinary forms of the
; language, so it inherits every value-kind those forms use — unions
; included. `:unioned` is `union{spot, target-ref}`, the way a colour
; attachment is either the canvas or a texture.
;
; `lowerOneForm` surface-validates the `(box …)` sub-tree before invoking
; the hook. That sub-tree's cross-ref index holds only `(box …)`, so `t`
; misses; both alternatives fail and the union reports
; `union_no_branch_matched` — a shape code, not one of the three cross-ref
; codes the gate used to excuse by name. The gate closed, the hook never
; ran, the container emitted nothing, and no diagnostic was produced at
; any stage. With `Options.defer_cross_refs` the fragment declines to
; adjudicate identity at all, the cross-ref alternative matches, and the
; hook runs.
;
; `(origin :ref b)` is what makes that observable in a corpus that
; compares diagnostics: `box-normal` exists only if the hook ran, so
; before the fix this file reported `not_cross_ref` at [origin ref].
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name target-ref :underlying symbol
    :cross-ref (cross-ref :target target))
  (value-kind :name spot :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [here]))
  (value-kind :name spot-or-target :underlying union
    :union (union-shape :alternatives [spot target-ref]))
  (value-kind :name child-item :underlying form
    :heads (head-set :names [child]))
  (value-kind :name box-ref :underlying symbol
    :cross-ref (cross-ref :target box-normal))

  (form :name target
    (key :name name :type symbol :optional false))
  (form :name child
    (key :name unioned :type spot-or-target :optional false))
  (form :name box
    (key :name name :type symbol :optional false)
    :positional child-item
    :lowering (lowering :hook test/identity-v1 :produces [box-normal]))
  (form :name box-normal
    (key :name name :type symbol :optional false))
  (form :name origin
    (key :name ref :type box-ref :optional false)))

(target :name t)
(box :name b (child :unioned t))
(origin :ref b)
